\tag{fdip}
\title{Positive interacting laws and controlled cumulants}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{A finite graph with massive Gaussian fields can be perturbed by a
nonnegative onsite quartic. Its [formal fiber interaction](fdip-005Y)
records the coefficients created when some vertices are removed.
For a positive real coupling, what probability law do those
coefficients describe, and how accurately do finitely many of them
approximate its retained interaction?}

\p{The Gaussian block formula in \ref{fdip-000D} fixes the conditional
reference and its volume factor. Positive weights then give exact
marginals on any orthogonally selected subspace. The
three-coordinate quartic in \ref{fdip-0047} gives a concrete comparison
between these integrals and their finite-order expansions.}

